---
/**
 * Product Safety (§8.6).
 *
 * Explains how Feytom handles specifications and documentation. §8.6 forbids
 * generalised rigging, tie-down or load-calculation instructions without
 * qualified technical review, so none appear here — this page is about our
 * publication policy, not about how to secure a load.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/global/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import SectionIntro from "../components/content/SectionIntro.astro";
import QuoteCtaPanel from "../components/content/QuoteCtaPanel.astro";
import { SAFETY_NOTE, SAFETY_NOTE_CONTEXT } from "../lib/safety";
import { ORGANIZATION, breadcrumbList } from "../lib/seo";
const crumbs = [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Product safety" }];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Product Safety & Documentation | Feytom"
  description="How Feytom handles product specifications, load limits and safety documentation, and what we will not publish until manufacturer documentation supports it."
  schema={[ORGANIZATION, breadcrumbList(crumbs)]}
>
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} /></div>

  <section class="section section--tight-top" aria-labelledby="ps-h">
    <div class="container ps">
      <SectionIntro
        id="ps-h" level={1}
        eyebrow="Product safety"
        heading="How we handle specifications and documentation"
        body="This page explains what we publish, what we withhold, and how to obtain technical documentation."
      />

      <div class="ps__note" role="note" aria-labelledby="ps-note-h">
        <h2 id="ps-note-h" class="t-eyebrow ps__note-h">Important product note</h2>
        <p class="ps__note-body">{SAFETY_NOTE}</p>
        <p class="t-small ps__note-ctx">{SAFETY_NOTE_CONTEXT}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ps__body">
        <h2 class="t-h2">Every figure carries its source</h2>
        <p class="t-body">
          Specifications on this site sit at one of three levels of evidence, and
          the level is shown next to the value rather than left for you to guess.
        </p>
        <ol class="ps__levels">
          <li>
            <strong>Confirmed.</strong> Observable on the product as supplied —
            diameter, length, material, colour, packaging. Shown plainly.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>As printed on the packaging.</strong> Figures Feytom publishes
            on its own retail packaging, reproduced here with that attribution
            visible. The Grade 70 chain's 4,700 lb working load limit is the
            current example. This is real published data, and it is weaker than a
            test certificate — which is why we name where it comes from instead of
            presenting it as our own measurement.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Manufacturer-verified.</strong> Backed by a spec sheet or test
            certificate. <em>We hold none yet.</em> When we do, those values will
            be labelled as such, and they will take precedence over packaging
            figures.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="t-h2">What we still withhold</h2>
        <p class="t-body">
          Anything that does not sit at one of those three levels is not published.
          That currently includes breaking strengths for every product, and any
          compliance claim naming an enforcement body.
        </p>
        <ul class="ps__list">
          <li>
            <strong>A bare marking is not a rating.</strong> The lashing belt
            carries a 3T marking. We publish it as a marking, because a stamped
            figure with no stated basis does not establish a working load limit.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A working load limit is not a breaking strength.</strong> The
            two are different numbers with different safety factors. We publish
            neither unless it is stated somewhere we can point to.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Marked for is not approved by.</strong> The Grade 70 chain is
            marked for DOT transport requirements. That describes the marking. It
            is not a statement that any authority has approved the product.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Applications are possible uses, not approvals.</strong> A use
            listed on a product page is not a statement that the product is
            approved for your specific load, equipment or method.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="t-h2">How to obtain technical documentation</h2>
        <p class="t-body">
          Ask for it in a quote request. Tell us the product and the application,
          and we will supply the manufacturer documentation we hold or tell you
          plainly that we do not yet hold it. Specification sheets will appear as
          downloads on product pages once approved documents are available.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h2">What this page is not</h2>
        <p class="t-body">
          It is not guidance on how to secure a load. Tie-down counts, load
          calculations, inspection intervals and rigging method depend on your
          equipment, your load and the regulations that apply to you. Those
          decisions need the manufacturer's instructions and qualified judgement,
          and this page is not a substitute for either.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteCtaPanel
    heading="Need the documentation before you order?"
    body="Ask for it in a quote request. Name the product and the application and we will tell you exactly what we hold."
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ps__note {
    border: var(--rule) solid var(--color-border);
    border-inline-start: var(--rule-heavy) solid var(--color-heading);
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-6);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }
  .ps__note-h { color: var(--color-heading); margin: 0; }
  .ps__note-body { margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-lg); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .ps__note-ctx { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .ps__body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .ps__body h2 { margin-block-start: var(--space-3); }
  .ps__body h2:first-child { margin-block-start: 0; }
  .ps__list, .ps__levels { margin: 0; padding-inline-start: var(--space-3); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1-5); }
  .ps__levels li { padding-inline-start: var(--space-0-5); }
  .ps__levels em { color: var(--color-pending); font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; }
  .ps__list strong, .ps__levels strong { color: var(--color-heading); }
</style>
